(Deep Residual Learning for Image Segmentation) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Abstract) Tj T*
(Medical image segmentation models often perform well on data from the) Tj T*
(same distribution as their training set. However, their performance may) Tj T*
(degrade when deployed in a different clinical environment. Domain shift) Tj T*
(refers to a change in the data distribution between source and target) Tj T*
(domains. In this paper we study this effect on three public datasets.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(1. Introduction) Tj T*
(Consider a model trained on images acquired at Hospital A. Images from) Tj T*
(Hospital B may differ in scanner settings, patient populations, or) Tj T*
(acquisition protocols. These differences can change image appearance) Tj T*
(without changing the underlying segmentation task.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
endobj
